WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.513 --> 00:00:01.998
- And I want to tell you passion,

00:00:01.998 --> 00:00:03.303
and from the heart,

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.220
always always wins over

00:00:07.589 --> 00:00:09.624
over-prepared and thinking from the head.

00:00:09.624 --> 00:00:10.610
Winston Churchill said,

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:14.923
"The definition of success is
going from failure to failure

00:00:14.923 --> 00:00:16.878
"without losing your enthusiasm."

00:00:16.878 --> 00:00:18.117
We think we have ADD.

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:19.403
Most of us don't have ADD.

00:00:19.403 --> 00:00:20.717
There's just too much coming at us,

00:00:20.717 --> 00:00:23.322
and we say yes to too many things.

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:24.459
- Hello, Believe Nation.

00:00:24.459 --> 00:00:25.379
I'm Evan Carmichael.

00:00:25.379 --> 00:00:27.012
My one word is believe,

00:00:27.012 --> 00:00:28.970
and I believe that
entrepreneurs are going to

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:31.809
solve all of the major
problems of the world.

00:00:31.809 --> 00:00:33.291
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:33.291 --> 00:00:34.423
today we're going to learn from

00:00:34.423 --> 00:00:36.591
real estate expert Dean Graziosi,

00:00:36.591 --> 00:00:39.645
and my take on his top
ten rules for success.

00:00:39.645 --> 00:00:41.348
Rule number three is my personal favorite,

00:00:41.348 --> 00:00:43.921
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:43.921 --> 00:00:45.356
And as always, guys, as you're watching,

00:00:45.356 --> 00:00:47.701
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:49.574
please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:00:49.574 --> 00:00:52.156
Put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired.

00:00:52.156 --> 00:00:53.927
And when you write it down

00:00:53.927 --> 00:00:57.147
it's much more likely to
stick for yourself as well.

00:00:57.147 --> 00:00:57.980
Enjoy.

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:04.561
(uplifting music playing)

00:01:10.888 --> 00:01:12.430
- Think about how many times in your life

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:15.818
you had a massive win because
you had no confidence.

00:01:15.818 --> 00:01:16.784
It doesn't exist.

00:01:16.784 --> 00:01:19.932
Right, if you're looking to
go meet that girl or that guy

00:01:19.932 --> 00:01:21.468
and you walked up and you're like,

00:01:21.468 --> 00:01:24.321
"Hey, um, you know I
was hoping we could...

00:01:24.321 --> 00:01:25.154
"can I get your--"

00:01:25.154 --> 00:01:26.349
No, that doesn't work!

00:01:26.349 --> 00:01:27.585
You walk into a business meeting.

00:01:27.585 --> 00:01:28.564
"Hey, do you think we could--"

00:01:28.564 --> 00:01:30.033
No, that doesn't work!

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:31.731
Go to talk to your kids
about something in school.

00:01:31.731 --> 00:01:32.564
"Hey kids, uh--"

00:01:32.564 --> 00:01:34.160
No! You need confidence.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.037
You need the energy.

00:01:35.037 --> 00:01:36.615
And you need to be alive.

00:01:36.615 --> 00:01:37.448
Well, if you know me,

00:01:37.448 --> 00:01:39.093
and been watching my videos, that's me.

00:01:39.093 --> 00:01:41.792
I've made my career on enthusiasm

00:01:41.792 --> 00:01:43.882
and energy and being in
the right state of mind

00:01:43.882 --> 00:01:45.036
and having the confidence.

00:01:45.036 --> 00:01:48.476
But the biggest myth is that
you're born with confidence.

00:01:48.476 --> 00:01:50.913
No, I was the shyest kid in the world.

00:01:50.913 --> 00:01:51.970
I felt so insecure.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:53.155
I felt dumb.

00:01:53.155 --> 00:01:55.495
I learned how to
manufacture the confidence.

00:01:55.495 --> 00:01:58.256
And after 25 years of
being an entrepreneur,

00:01:58.256 --> 00:01:59.822
generating hundreds of
millions of dollars,

00:01:59.822 --> 00:02:01.178
being blessed to touch the lives

00:02:01.178 --> 00:02:03.648
of millions of people around the world,

00:02:03.648 --> 00:02:05.646
what I know for a fact

00:02:05.646 --> 00:02:08.047
is that you can create the state of mind

00:02:08.047 --> 00:02:10.383
and the confidence to live the best you.

00:02:10.383 --> 00:02:11.907
To unlock that inner hero.

00:02:11.907 --> 00:02:15.000
I literally flew to Arizona
to meet a media-buyer

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.437
and I said, "I have no
idea what I'm doing."

00:02:16.437 --> 00:02:17.765
And I just kept pushing in.

00:02:17.765 --> 00:02:20.516
And one of those things that I think

00:02:20.516 --> 00:02:22.496
during the evolution of growing

00:02:22.496 --> 00:02:24.848
from wherever you are
to where you want to go,

00:02:24.848 --> 00:02:27.415
is do whatever you do best.

00:02:27.415 --> 00:02:30.668
I mean do whatever you're
doing the best you can,

00:02:30.668 --> 00:02:33.166
knowing there's the bigger horizon.

00:02:33.166 --> 00:02:35.842
So, I literally was working
during the day on cars.

00:02:35.842 --> 00:02:37.271
I'd paint cars.

00:02:37.271 --> 00:02:38.267
I was doing collision repair.

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:40.031
At night I'd go work on my apartments,

00:02:40.031 --> 00:02:41.121
and I was a plumber,

00:02:41.121 --> 00:02:43.033
and hung sheetrock.

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:44.448
And I'd work till midnight on houses.

00:02:44.448 --> 00:02:45.811
And I was tired.

00:02:45.811 --> 00:02:46.883
But I had a dream.

00:02:46.883 --> 00:02:49.327
I knew I wanted to help people do better.

00:02:49.327 --> 00:02:51.234
So, it made what I was doing okay

00:02:51.234 --> 00:02:53.573
because I knew there was more.

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:55.652
So the big problem I
see is people want more

00:02:55.652 --> 00:02:57.773
and they hate what they're doing.

00:02:57.773 --> 00:03:00.414
So they're in a state of mind where,

00:03:00.414 --> 00:03:01.929
"God, just when I'm done with this crap

00:03:01.929 --> 00:03:03.660
"then someday I'll reach my dreams."

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.078
And if you can flop that to go,

00:03:05.078 --> 00:03:07.231
"No, this is the gateway to my dreams.

00:03:07.231 --> 00:03:08.685
"I don't care that I'm serving coffee,

00:03:08.685 --> 00:03:09.702
"or I'm painting cars,

00:03:09.702 --> 00:03:10.950
"or I'm a teacher right now,

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:12.924
"or I'm on my sister's couch.

00:03:12.924 --> 00:03:14.215
"This is what I have to do

00:03:14.215 --> 00:03:15.118
"and I have to do it the best."

00:03:15.118 --> 00:03:15.996
- [Interviewer] Become a master at this.

00:03:15.996 --> 00:03:17.154
- Just become a master at that,

00:03:17.154 --> 00:03:19.384
and that's the income and the security

00:03:19.384 --> 00:03:22.733
and the mindset that fuels the next level.

00:03:22.733 --> 00:03:24.353
It's not, "This is miserable, I hate it.

00:03:24.353 --> 00:03:25.259
"I fueled the next level,

00:03:25.259 --> 00:03:26.312
"and now I'm amazing."

00:03:26.312 --> 00:03:28.455
It's like, you need to master that.

00:03:28.455 --> 00:03:29.450
- [Interviewer] Yeah, the process.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:30.399
- Yeah.

00:03:30.399 --> 00:03:32.179
You know, I know I've gone onstage

00:03:32.179 --> 00:03:34.450
in front of 10 thousand people,

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:37.091
and I thought I should
have more PowerPoint.

00:03:37.091 --> 00:03:38.200
I should have more reminders.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.807
And I just remember
walking out and saying,

00:03:40.807 --> 00:03:43.598
"I'm here to help rise these people up,

00:03:43.598 --> 00:03:45.873
"to give them capabilities
to change their life.

00:03:45.873 --> 00:03:49.465
"It's my vision, it's my
goal, it's my obligation

00:03:49.465 --> 00:03:52.231
"to use my unique ability
to just help these people

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:53.441
"and live from my heart."

00:03:53.441 --> 00:03:54.445
And all I could think about is

00:03:54.445 --> 00:03:55.654
changing these people's lives.

00:03:55.654 --> 00:03:56.565
And when I got out there,

00:03:56.565 --> 00:03:58.426
I wasn't perfect onstage.

00:03:58.426 --> 00:04:01.035
I wasn't robotic and say the right things

00:04:01.035 --> 00:04:02.858
and I didn't have the
crisp, clear PowerPoint.

00:04:02.858 --> 00:04:04.456
But when I spoke from the heart,

00:04:04.456 --> 00:04:06.127
it overcame all of that.

00:04:06.127 --> 00:04:08.547
And I get to be one of the
best presenters wherever I go

00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:10.279
because I speak from the heart.

00:04:10.279 --> 00:04:11.112
Now you might be saying,

00:04:11.112 --> 00:04:11.945
"Dean, that's your unique ability."

00:04:11.945 --> 00:04:13.387
And maybe that is.

00:04:13.387 --> 00:04:15.189
But I know for you in life

00:04:15.189 --> 00:04:18.590
there are circumstances
where you have to prepare,

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:19.816
you have to do a PowerPoint,

00:04:19.816 --> 00:04:21.113
you have to do a presentation.

00:04:21.113 --> 00:04:22.285
And I want to tell you,

00:04:22.285 --> 00:04:25.618
passion and from the heart always always

00:04:27.441 --> 00:04:30.712
wins over over-prepared
and thinking from the head.

00:04:30.712 --> 00:04:31.913
Let me just ask you something.

00:04:31.913 --> 00:04:34.264
Right now in the crazy presidential race,

00:04:34.264 --> 00:04:35.560
the GOP race,

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:38.288
Ben Carson is probably the smartest guy,

00:04:38.288 --> 00:04:39.524
when it comes to book smart,

00:04:39.524 --> 00:04:41.838
out of the whole group.

00:04:41.838 --> 00:04:42.809
And I don't watch the news a lot,

00:04:42.809 --> 00:04:43.861
but I just read a lot,

00:04:43.861 --> 00:04:45.563
and somebody said this the other day

00:04:45.563 --> 00:04:47.223
and it just hit me.

00:04:47.223 --> 00:04:48.795
Someone said, "Man, Ben Carson is probably

00:04:48.795 --> 00:04:52.268
"the smartest guy in that
GOP race that's going on."

00:04:52.268 --> 00:04:53.101
Whatever you think of it.

00:04:53.101 --> 00:04:55.714
I'm not going to share my opinion.

00:04:55.714 --> 00:04:56.631
You know what the guy
said when he was done?

00:04:56.631 --> 00:04:58.016
He's like, "But we all know

00:04:58.016 --> 00:05:00.241
"the smartest guy never wins."

00:05:00.241 --> 00:05:02.207
And I was like, "Wow.

00:05:02.207 --> 00:05:06.006
"We all know that the
smartest guy never wins?

00:05:06.006 --> 00:05:07.564
"What does that mean?"

00:05:07.564 --> 00:05:09.383
And it's kind of what I'm sharing today.

00:05:09.383 --> 00:05:10.497
I'm not saying you shouldn't be smart.

00:05:10.497 --> 00:05:13.507
So many of you are probably
way smarter than I am.

00:05:13.507 --> 00:05:16.342
But what I want to tell you
is enthusiasm and passion

00:05:16.342 --> 00:05:17.997
and living from your heart,

00:05:17.997 --> 00:05:20.223
to me, 100% of the time,

00:05:20.223 --> 00:05:23.512
outweighs being over-prepared and robotic

00:05:23.512 --> 00:05:25.145
and trying to think what to say.

00:05:25.145 --> 00:05:27.363
I hope I'm getting the
right message across today.

00:05:27.363 --> 00:05:29.976
Cause I've had this question
from so many people.

00:05:29.976 --> 00:05:32.523
How are you so easy to
talk on camera, onstage?

00:05:32.523 --> 00:05:34.188
And I never have a good answer.

00:05:34.188 --> 00:05:35.104
And I really thought through it.

00:05:35.104 --> 00:05:36.513
And that's the answer.

00:05:36.513 --> 00:05:39.289
I am here right now
doing this video for you

00:05:39.289 --> 00:05:41.995
because each week I want
to deliver you a nugget

00:05:41.995 --> 00:05:43.328
that you can just place into your life

00:05:43.328 --> 00:05:45.343
and make a tiny shift
towards a better life.

00:05:45.343 --> 00:05:46.877
So I don't need a teleprompter.

00:05:46.877 --> 00:05:47.934
I don't need a script.

00:05:47.934 --> 00:05:50.059
I come here and just want to deliver,

00:05:50.059 --> 00:05:51.504
and it's coming from my heart.

00:05:51.504 --> 00:05:52.384
Now, I have practiced.

00:05:52.384 --> 00:05:54.040
I've been on video for 15 years.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.653
I've been doing these
for seven, eight years.

00:05:56.653 --> 00:05:58.478
And maybe that's not what you do,

00:05:58.478 --> 00:06:01.511
but you're still going to
have these circumstances

00:06:01.511 --> 00:06:02.837
where you have to talk to your children,

00:06:02.837 --> 00:06:03.799
talk to your co-workers,

00:06:03.799 --> 00:06:04.829
talk to your employees,

00:06:04.829 --> 00:06:06.631
and talk to your employer.

00:06:06.631 --> 00:06:08.147
And if you get stuck in your head,

00:06:08.147 --> 00:06:09.058
that's when you get stressed,

00:06:09.058 --> 00:06:10.175
that's when you get worried,

00:06:10.175 --> 00:06:11.578
that's when you try to
remember what to say.

00:06:11.578 --> 00:06:13.766
You leave and go, "Oh,
why did I say that?"

00:06:13.766 --> 00:06:15.907
Or "Why didn't I say more?"

00:06:15.907 --> 00:06:16.783
But if you can go in

00:06:16.783 --> 00:06:18.995
and say, "Why am I going in?"

00:06:18.995 --> 00:06:21.708
And live with passion and
have it come from your heart,

00:06:21.708 --> 00:06:22.764
then that's truly you,

00:06:22.764 --> 00:06:24.548
and you're giving the
answers you're supposed to

00:06:24.548 --> 00:06:25.694
from the real you.

00:06:25.694 --> 00:06:28.672
Not the facade that
sometimes life makes us wear.

00:06:28.672 --> 00:06:30.963
We have this ideal, this image,

00:06:30.963 --> 00:06:32.620
that everything has to be great.

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:34.179
That we don't want any problems

00:06:34.179 --> 00:06:35.912
because we're supposed
to be happy all the time.

00:06:35.912 --> 00:06:36.820
We're supposed to be fulfilled.

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:38.116
We're supposed to be full of joy.

00:06:38.116 --> 00:06:39.446
And nothing's supposed to go wrong.

00:06:39.446 --> 00:06:41.994
But the problems are what make us have

00:06:41.994 --> 00:06:43.700
the other side of happiness.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:45.028
The harder our problems,

00:06:45.028 --> 00:06:47.550
and the way we find solutions,

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.460
the way we overcome those problems,

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:52.372
the way we process them: be
sad, be hurt, be annoyed,

00:06:52.372 --> 00:06:55.271
and push it out, learn from them, move on.

00:06:55.271 --> 00:06:58.549
The level of our problems
the level of our success.

00:06:58.549 --> 00:07:00.750
You know, you might want
to be in a rock band,

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:03.213
and you want to know the
feel of being up onstage

00:07:03.213 --> 00:07:05.966
and having all these people
loving you and cheering.

00:07:05.966 --> 00:07:09.125
But if you don't want to
go through the practices,

00:07:09.125 --> 00:07:10.959
and the rehearsals,
and carrying your stuff

00:07:10.959 --> 00:07:13.546
in and out of dumpy little bars,

00:07:13.546 --> 00:07:15.153
and stuff like that all those years,

00:07:15.153 --> 00:07:17.773
then you don't want to take
on that problem of learning

00:07:17.773 --> 00:07:21.019
in order to have the
reward for being onstage

00:07:21.019 --> 00:07:22.365
and being a musician, right?

00:07:22.365 --> 00:07:23.963
If you want to start your own company

00:07:23.963 --> 00:07:25.155
and you just want to make the money

00:07:25.155 --> 00:07:26.143
and drive the fancy cars

00:07:26.143 --> 00:07:27.919
like some of these websites you see,

00:07:27.919 --> 00:07:28.799
the billion-dollar website and

00:07:28.799 --> 00:07:30.485
a bunch of people flashing money.

00:07:30.485 --> 00:07:33.087
It makes you think, "I
want all that happiness,

00:07:33.087 --> 00:07:35.092
"but I don't want the
problems to get there."

00:07:35.092 --> 00:07:37.015
Listen, that old saying:

00:07:37.015 --> 00:07:41.226
the smoothest rock is in the
roughest part of the stream.

00:07:41.226 --> 00:07:43.205
If you've had problems,

00:07:43.205 --> 00:07:45.643
if you are having a problem in your life,

00:07:45.643 --> 00:07:47.860
how you overcome that problem,

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:49.744
how you figure out solutions

00:07:49.744 --> 00:07:52.886
is the level of life that you get to live.

00:07:52.886 --> 00:07:53.719
Somebody told me once,

00:07:53.719 --> 00:07:57.064
"The level of complexity you can handle,

00:07:57.064 --> 00:07:59.007
"correlates, in so many
ways, to the amount of money

00:07:59.007 --> 00:08:00.757
and the happiness you can achieve."

00:08:00.757 --> 00:08:03.347
And, again, I share this
with my kids all the time,

00:08:03.347 --> 00:08:05.239
you don't know tall until you know short.

00:08:05.239 --> 00:08:07.738
You don't know happy unless you know sad.

00:08:07.738 --> 00:08:10.140
You don't know cloudy days
unless you know sunny days

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:11.028
and vice versa.

00:08:11.028 --> 00:08:13.297
So, what I'm sharing with you is,

00:08:13.297 --> 00:08:15.752
your problems are here to sharpen us.

00:08:15.752 --> 00:08:18.188
Your problems are here
to make us stronger.

00:08:18.188 --> 00:08:21.580
Your problems are here
to find the solutions,

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:24.021
and the more problems you can take on,

00:08:24.021 --> 00:08:25.816
the more problems you can get through

00:08:25.816 --> 00:08:27.703
and come out strong on the other side,

00:08:27.703 --> 00:08:30.063
the faster your life will
go to the next level.

00:08:30.063 --> 00:08:33.603
Winston Churchill said,
"The definition of success

00:08:33.603 --> 00:08:35.956
"is going from failure to failure

00:08:35.956 --> 00:08:37.866
"without losing your enthusiasm."

00:08:37.866 --> 00:08:38.829
Take it one step further.

00:08:38.829 --> 00:08:42.363
From problems to obstacles
that you can overcome.

00:08:42.363 --> 00:08:43.196
They make you stronger.

00:08:43.196 --> 00:08:44.960
They make you have more grit.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:47.026
And you have the ability
to go to the next level.

00:08:47.026 --> 00:08:49.175
Don't try to avoid problems.

00:08:49.175 --> 00:08:50.242
Fix those problems.

00:08:50.242 --> 00:08:51.075
Get through it.

00:08:51.075 --> 00:08:52.020
Find a solution.

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:54.805
And watch yourself just step
up the ladder of success,

00:08:54.805 --> 00:08:55.712
whether it's real estate,

00:08:55.712 --> 00:08:57.124
whether it's success in your own life,

00:08:57.124 --> 00:08:59.357
your happiness, your joy, your abundance.

00:08:59.357 --> 00:09:01.937
You have the opportunity to
look at problems differently,

00:09:01.937 --> 00:09:05.014
as a blessing, as a gift,
as hard as some of them are,

00:09:05.014 --> 00:09:06.765
get over them and hit that next level.

00:09:06.765 --> 00:09:07.685
The one you deserve.

00:09:07.685 --> 00:09:08.716
I hit it big in real estate by the time

00:09:08.716 --> 00:09:10.695
I was 26, 27 years old

00:09:10.695 --> 00:09:11.580
just by taking action.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:12.932
Knocking on a million doors

00:09:12.932 --> 00:09:14.619
and finally got somebody
to do a no-money-down deal

00:09:14.619 --> 00:09:15.926
with me when I was 20.

00:09:15.926 --> 00:09:16.759
Then another one.

00:09:16.759 --> 00:09:18.230
And I rolled that into the
next deal and next deal.

00:09:18.230 --> 00:09:19.299
- Consistent action.

00:09:19.299 --> 00:09:20.943
- Consistent action.

00:09:20.943 --> 00:09:22.866
And consistent failing and
getting back up, right?

00:09:22.866 --> 00:09:25.736
The space between failures is really

00:09:25.736 --> 00:09:28.108
a huge determining factor
of your success, right?

00:09:28.108 --> 00:09:29.304
It's like if you can fail fast,

00:09:29.304 --> 00:09:30.455
you can win quicker.

00:09:30.455 --> 00:09:31.324
- Yeah.

00:09:31.324 --> 00:09:33.339
- How can you find the time, the energy,

00:09:33.339 --> 00:09:36.534
the effort, and the nerve to start?

00:09:36.534 --> 00:09:38.290
To make that first call.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:39.779
To put out that first bandit sign.

00:09:39.779 --> 00:09:41.060
To put up a craigslist ad.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:42.680
To start to 25 to one.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:43.973
To call banks.

00:09:43.973 --> 00:09:45.085
How do you do that?

00:09:45.085 --> 00:09:49.109
Well, this one today
is learning to say no.

00:09:49.109 --> 00:09:50.974
Now, one thing I've learned from

00:09:50.974 --> 00:09:52.501
the most successful people on the planet,

00:09:52.501 --> 00:09:53.780
if you want to say millionaires,

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:55.420
I've been lucky enough
to meet billionaires.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:57.253
The one thing I've learned,

00:09:57.253 --> 00:09:59.376
the more they say no,

00:09:59.376 --> 00:10:00.912
the wealthier they get.

00:10:00.912 --> 00:10:02.557
Now, you may have heard
me say this before,

00:10:02.557 --> 00:10:05.071
but it's that important
of a success principle.

00:10:05.071 --> 00:10:07.771
It took you a lot of yes's to get here.

00:10:07.771 --> 00:10:08.604
Yes to overtime.

00:10:08.604 --> 00:10:12.533
Yes to missing your kid's
soccer or dance class.

00:10:12.533 --> 00:10:13.821
Yes to your wife, your
husband getting upset

00:10:13.821 --> 00:10:15.146
cause you're working late.

00:10:15.146 --> 00:10:16.769
Or yes to getting my program.

00:10:16.769 --> 00:10:18.166
Yes to going to a live event.

00:10:18.166 --> 00:10:19.532
Yes to getting the education.

00:10:19.532 --> 00:10:20.625
Yes, yes, yes.

00:10:20.625 --> 00:10:22.300
Yes to your friends.

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:23.133
If you're watching this,

00:10:23.133 --> 00:10:25.151
you are the busiest
people other people know.

00:10:25.151 --> 00:10:27.022
They say if you want something
done, ask somebody busy

00:10:27.022 --> 00:10:28.289
cause they know how to get things done.

00:10:28.289 --> 00:10:29.173
That's you.

00:10:29.173 --> 00:10:31.061
You're the person in your
family, amongst your friends,

00:10:31.061 --> 00:10:32.843
I know it or else you
wouldn't be watching me,

00:10:32.843 --> 00:10:34.135
that get asked for emotional support,

00:10:34.135 --> 00:10:37.772
financial support, for a
ride, for help, for advice.

00:10:37.772 --> 00:10:40.414
So you are used to saying yes.

00:10:40.414 --> 00:10:42.495
So this week I want you to say no.

00:10:42.495 --> 00:10:44.553
I want you to make the list of the things

00:10:44.553 --> 00:10:48.413
that you must say no to
so you can focus on you.

00:10:48.413 --> 00:10:50.752
So you can make a massive
impact for your family.

00:10:50.752 --> 00:10:52.961
You want to help family
members that need money?

00:10:52.961 --> 00:10:54.522
Say no to them for a year,

00:10:54.522 --> 00:10:57.223
become an incredible real estate investor,

00:10:57.223 --> 00:10:59.707
and then if you want to
cut them checks, you can.

00:10:59.707 --> 00:11:00.968
If you want to give more to your church,

00:11:00.968 --> 00:11:02.434
you want to give more to charity,

00:11:02.434 --> 00:11:05.151
say no for a little
while to so many things,

00:11:05.151 --> 00:11:06.919
so your brain's not all over the place.

00:11:06.919 --> 00:11:08.098
We think we have ADD.

00:11:08.098 --> 00:11:09.484
Most of us don't have ADD,

00:11:09.484 --> 00:11:11.328
there's just too much coming at us,

00:11:11.328 --> 00:11:13.354
and we say yes to too many things.

00:11:13.354 --> 00:11:15.128
So here is the assignment.

00:11:15.128 --> 00:11:17.707
What can you figure out
to say no to this week?

00:11:17.707 --> 00:11:19.650
Because if you say no to things

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:21.040
that don't improve your life,

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:22.253
don't improve your family's life,

00:11:22.253 --> 00:11:24.840
don't possibly increase
your future income,

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.175
or put you on the path to
the goals that you have,

00:11:27.175 --> 00:11:28.754
to spend more time with your family,

00:11:28.754 --> 00:11:29.643
to get out of a job you hate,

00:11:29.643 --> 00:11:30.676
to pay off bills.

00:11:30.676 --> 00:11:31.710
I don't know what they are,

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:33.390
but you have to make,

00:11:33.390 --> 00:11:34.628
not a to-do list,

00:11:34.628 --> 00:11:37.183
but you have to make a
list of what not to do.

00:11:37.183 --> 00:11:38.554
Who are you going to say no to?

00:11:38.554 --> 00:11:40.578
Who are you going to disappoint?

00:11:40.578 --> 00:11:41.963
What are you going to let go?

00:11:41.963 --> 00:11:43.678
What habits are eating up your time?

00:11:43.678 --> 00:11:46.595
Kaizen, the study of kaizen,

00:11:46.595 --> 00:11:49.257
is one little piece at a time.

00:11:49.257 --> 00:11:50.534
That's how to eat an elephant,

00:11:50.534 --> 00:11:51.451
one bite at a time.

00:11:51.451 --> 00:11:53.715
How do you run a thousand-mile race?

00:11:53.715 --> 00:11:55.132
One step at a time.

00:11:55.132 --> 00:11:57.479
When Japan rebuilt after World War Two,

00:11:57.479 --> 00:12:00.412
they had to adapt kaizen cause
everything was destroyed.

00:12:00.412 --> 00:12:01.796
They looked at everything gone.

00:12:01.796 --> 00:12:03.913
They couldn't imagine
trying to rebuild Japan.

00:12:03.913 --> 00:12:04.789
But what did they do?

00:12:04.789 --> 00:12:06.948
They built it one brick at a time,

00:12:06.948 --> 00:12:08.155
one person at a time,

00:12:08.155 --> 00:12:09.579
one business at a time.

00:12:09.579 --> 00:12:12.978
It turned into such a
thriving country so fast

00:12:12.978 --> 00:12:14.554
cause they adapted kaizen.

00:12:14.554 --> 00:12:15.786
Break it up into small pieces.

00:12:15.786 --> 00:12:16.619
You got a goal?

00:12:16.619 --> 00:12:18.993
Take a bite today, this moment.

00:12:18.993 --> 00:12:20.315
When you're done watching us right now,

00:12:20.315 --> 00:12:22.108
go do something towards your goal.

00:12:22.108 --> 00:12:23.531
Go send an email.

00:12:23.531 --> 00:12:24.364
Call somebody.

00:12:24.364 --> 00:12:25.197
Say no.

00:12:25.197 --> 00:12:26.030
Say yes.

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:26.863
Look for a new job.

00:12:26.863 --> 00:12:27.735
Start the company.

00:12:27.735 --> 00:12:29.291
Create the URL.

00:12:29.291 --> 00:12:31.042
If it's real estate, go make offers.

00:12:31.042 --> 00:12:33.080
The only reason you think about money

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:36.121
is cause there's not enough
flowing into your life.

00:12:36.121 --> 00:12:37.592
Because when money flows into your life,

00:12:37.592 --> 00:12:39.869
you get to be your best you.

00:12:39.869 --> 00:12:41.348
And the only reason I'm sharing that is

00:12:41.348 --> 00:12:44.695
cause so many people have
this deep-seated fear

00:12:44.695 --> 00:12:45.984
of making extra money.

00:12:45.984 --> 00:12:48.016
Listen, if you can cut
a check for a problem,

00:12:48.016 --> 00:12:50.705
you don't have that damn problem anymore.

00:12:50.705 --> 00:12:52.120
You worry about your
kids, you can cut a check.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:53.329
You're worrying about credit card bills,

00:12:53.329 --> 00:12:54.162
worrying about your business,

00:12:54.162 --> 00:12:54.995
worrying about your parents,

00:12:54.995 --> 00:12:56.462
if you can cut a check for that problem,

00:12:56.462 --> 00:12:58.059
does it solve the problem?

00:12:58.059 --> 00:12:59.183
We still have to work on us.

00:12:59.183 --> 00:13:00.054
It doesn't fix us,

00:13:00.054 --> 00:13:01.525
but it solves a lot of problems.

00:13:01.525 --> 00:13:04.134
So when I ask you why you
want to make more money,

00:13:04.134 --> 00:13:05.308
why you want to diversify,

00:13:05.308 --> 00:13:07.298
why you want to have a
new stream of income,

00:13:07.298 --> 00:13:09.817
I just want to give you
this little example.

00:13:09.817 --> 00:13:13.441
I hired a consultant to help
me be better with my students,

00:13:13.441 --> 00:13:15.685
get more people engaged to take action.

00:13:15.685 --> 00:13:17.284
He said to me, he sits down
for two minutes, he goes,

00:13:17.284 --> 00:13:19.769
"Well, did you ever teach
them the seven levels deep

00:13:19.769 --> 00:13:21.254
"of why they're doing it?"

00:13:21.254 --> 00:13:22.459
I said, "No, but if it helps them,

00:13:22.459 --> 00:13:23.292
"give it to me."

00:13:23.292 --> 00:13:24.981
He's like, "No, you have
to go through it or else

00:13:24.981 --> 00:13:25.814
"I won't give it to you."

00:13:25.814 --> 00:13:27.077
I said, "Fine, I'll go through it."

00:13:27.077 --> 00:13:28.141
So the whole thing is,

00:13:28.141 --> 00:13:29.614
I'm going to wrap this up quick,

00:13:29.614 --> 00:13:31.599
is whatever answer you said when I said,

00:13:31.599 --> 00:13:33.996
"Why do you want to make more money?"

00:13:33.996 --> 00:13:36.563
Ask the same question
again with that answer.

00:13:36.563 --> 00:13:38.742
So my first answer was,

00:13:38.742 --> 00:13:41.081
I want to have an incredible company

00:13:41.081 --> 00:13:43.993
that changes the world
while I make great money

00:13:43.993 --> 00:13:45.648
and can help other people.

00:13:45.648 --> 00:13:46.519
That was my first answer.

00:13:46.519 --> 00:13:47.396
Sounds noble, right?

00:13:47.396 --> 00:13:48.815
Sounds like, that's all from the brain.

00:13:48.815 --> 00:13:49.673
That's solid.

00:13:49.673 --> 00:13:50.506
That's who we are.

00:13:50.506 --> 00:13:52.252
We got this company, we're
going to change the world.

00:13:52.252 --> 00:13:53.576
But then he said to me, "Dean,

00:13:53.576 --> 00:13:56.294
"why is that important for you?"

00:13:56.294 --> 00:13:58.729
With my answer, why is
it important for you

00:13:58.729 --> 00:14:00.737
to have a solid business,
to help change lives,

00:14:00.737 --> 00:14:02.208
to make the money?

00:14:02.208 --> 00:14:04.732
Then I gave another
message from my head of,

00:14:04.732 --> 00:14:07.936
"Well, I want to set the
standard for my industry

00:14:07.936 --> 00:14:09.115
"and get rid of all the crap."

00:14:09.115 --> 00:14:10.680
And I did about four or five answers,

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:12.107
so I want you to do this tonight,

00:14:12.107 --> 00:14:13.715
go through this seven times.

00:14:13.715 --> 00:14:15.166
But what happens around the fourth time

00:14:15.166 --> 00:14:16.566
you ask yourself that question,

00:14:16.566 --> 00:14:19.658
you flop from your head to your heart.

00:14:19.658 --> 00:14:21.209
So I got to the third one,

00:14:21.209 --> 00:14:23.816
and I said, "I never
want to go backwards."

00:14:23.816 --> 00:14:25.488
Don't even know where it came from.

00:14:25.488 --> 00:14:28.448
As a kid, we were broke as crap.

00:14:28.448 --> 00:14:29.566
I wore hand-me-downs.

00:14:29.566 --> 00:14:30.882
I got dropped off far from school

00:14:30.882 --> 00:14:33.370
so the kids wouldn't make
fun of my mom's junkie car.

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:34.639
I was homeless at one point,

00:14:34.639 --> 00:14:36.099
where my parents had no place to go.

00:14:36.099 --> 00:14:37.099
I'd lie and tell my friends,

00:14:37.099 --> 00:14:38.301
I had no money at school,

00:14:38.301 --> 00:14:40.414
I'd tell them that I
didn't feel like eating

00:14:40.414 --> 00:14:42.509
cause my mom didn't have the
buck so I could eat that day.

00:14:42.509 --> 00:14:43.809
And that's not 'poor me.'

00:14:43.809 --> 00:14:44.642
That shaped me.

00:14:44.642 --> 00:14:45.475
I love every bit of it.

00:14:45.475 --> 00:14:46.955
But I hated it,

00:14:46.955 --> 00:14:48.685
and I realized I didn't
want to go backwards.

00:14:48.685 --> 00:14:50.505
I said, "That's it."

00:14:50.505 --> 00:14:52.501
And he said to me, "No,
Dean, we're not done.

00:14:52.501 --> 00:14:53.926
"It's seven levels deep, not five.

00:14:53.926 --> 00:14:57.238
"So, why don't you want to go backwards?"

00:14:57.238 --> 00:14:58.265
And it just hit me.

00:14:58.265 --> 00:14:59.098
And I remember I got emotional,

00:14:59.098 --> 00:14:59.931
I got goosebumps.

00:14:59.931 --> 00:15:00.884
I said, "I never want my kids to

00:15:00.884 --> 00:15:01.853
"experience what I went through.

00:15:01.853 --> 00:15:03.165
"I don't want to raise entitled kids,

00:15:03.165 --> 00:15:04.788
"but I want them to have options."

00:15:04.788 --> 00:15:06.322
I'm like, "That's it, I'm done."

00:15:06.322 --> 00:15:08.849
And he's like, "No, there's one more."

00:15:08.849 --> 00:15:09.682
I'm like, "What there could be?"

00:15:09.682 --> 00:15:10.515
And it just hit me.

00:15:10.515 --> 00:15:11.614
I said, "I want to be
in control of my life."

00:15:11.614 --> 00:15:14.038
My parents got married five times each.

00:15:14.038 --> 00:15:15.688
If you're military or you moved a lot,

00:15:15.688 --> 00:15:16.521
you know what it's like,

00:15:16.521 --> 00:15:18.014
every time you have
friends, family, new school,

00:15:18.014 --> 00:15:18.850
you got to move.

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:20.594
I moved 20 times by the time I was 19.

00:15:20.594 --> 00:15:23.651
And I just realized at that very moment,

00:15:23.651 --> 00:15:25.002
I wanted to be in control of my life.

00:15:25.002 --> 00:15:25.988
I wanted to dress the way I want.

00:15:25.988 --> 00:15:27.301
I wanted to do the work I wanted to work.

00:15:27.301 --> 00:15:29.162
I wanted to raise my
kids the way I wanted.

00:15:29.162 --> 00:15:31.638
No one was going to tell me
what to do in my adult life.

00:15:31.638 --> 00:15:33.365
And that was my why.

00:15:33.365 --> 00:15:34.542
If you're having a tough day,

00:15:34.542 --> 00:15:35.983
your business is kicking your ass,

00:15:35.983 --> 00:15:37.611
and you just think you want

00:15:37.611 --> 00:15:40.014
financial support or financial freedom,

00:15:40.014 --> 00:15:42.093
it's not enough to get
through a tough day.

00:15:42.093 --> 00:15:43.748
But when you know your true why.

00:15:43.748 --> 00:15:46.077
I went onstage for years
doing this week after week.

00:15:46.077 --> 00:15:47.934
And I had a woman come up.

00:15:47.934 --> 00:15:50.085
A woman, yesterday, said
she wanted to make money

00:15:50.085 --> 00:15:51.118
to travel the world.

00:15:51.118 --> 00:15:52.711
It reminded me of a woman that came up.

00:15:52.711 --> 00:15:56.120
Her first why was, "I
want to travel the world."

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:58.047
After seven levels deep,

00:15:58.047 --> 00:15:59.043
she got to number one.

00:15:59.043 --> 00:16:00.246
You know what she said?

00:16:00.246 --> 00:16:02.582
She goes, "My physically
abusive husband left me

00:16:02.582 --> 00:16:04.035
"two years ago.

00:16:04.035 --> 00:16:06.812
"On the way out the door he
said you're a pathetic loser.

00:16:06.812 --> 00:16:08.146
"You'll never amount to anything."

00:16:08.146 --> 00:16:09.834
And she goes, "I'm
going to show him wrong.

00:16:09.834 --> 00:16:10.813
"Screw him."

00:16:10.813 --> 00:16:12.395
That was her why.

00:16:12.395 --> 00:16:14.506
Is that a stronger why than just

00:16:14.506 --> 00:16:16.054
wanting to travel the world?

00:16:16.054 --> 00:16:17.458
I had another guy stand up and he said,

00:16:17.458 --> 00:16:21.025
"I want to change the
youth in my neighborhood.

00:16:21.025 --> 00:16:22.629
"There's not a lot of dads, no support.

00:16:22.629 --> 00:16:23.671
"I want to create this company.

00:16:23.671 --> 00:16:24.895
"I've already started making money.

00:16:24.895 --> 00:16:26.200
"I'm going to take it to the next level."

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:28.217
What a strong why coming from his head.

00:16:28.217 --> 00:16:30.176
You know what his number one was?

00:16:30.176 --> 00:16:32.487
That his mom died before she knew that

00:16:32.487 --> 00:16:34.251
she set a good example,

00:16:34.251 --> 00:16:36.504
and he felt he showed her he was a loser

00:16:36.504 --> 00:16:37.505
while she was alive.

00:16:37.505 --> 00:16:40.849
And he was going to show her
he was a winner in her death.

00:16:40.849 --> 00:16:42.781
Is that an incredible why?

00:16:42.781 --> 00:16:43.964
I'm talking about these two and

00:16:43.964 --> 00:16:46.340
I've been blessed to meet
presidents, multiple presidents,

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:47.476
I've met billionaires,

00:16:47.476 --> 00:16:49.331
I've been lucky to meet a lot of people,

00:16:49.331 --> 00:16:50.861
and I feel honored and blessed.

00:16:50.861 --> 00:16:53.861
But all of them have a humbleness of

00:16:56.958 --> 00:16:58.406
felt they weren't ready

00:16:58.406 --> 00:17:01.489
and not as good as you perceive them.

00:17:02.396 --> 00:17:03.350
Okay, I'll give you an example.

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:06.600
Derek said he went to England to study.

00:17:07.872 --> 00:17:11.915
And about four weeks before
the world championship,

00:17:11.915 --> 00:17:14.605
his coach came to him
and said, "Get ready.

00:17:14.605 --> 00:17:16.614
"In two weeks you're doing a competition.

00:17:16.614 --> 00:17:18.652
"If you win that and qualify,

00:17:18.652 --> 00:17:20.316
you're going to the world championship."

00:17:20.316 --> 00:17:21.920
And he said, "I'm not ready.

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:22.961
"Four weeks?

00:17:22.961 --> 00:17:23.872
"I'm not ready."

00:17:23.872 --> 00:17:25.773
He thought he was going the year after,

00:17:25.773 --> 00:17:27.354
and she said, "You're ready for it."

00:17:27.354 --> 00:17:30.052
He said he pined over
it and said, "No way.

00:17:30.052 --> 00:17:30.885
"I'm not ready."

00:17:30.885 --> 00:17:31.718
And she told him.

00:17:31.718 --> 00:17:33.891
And the cool part is he had a good mentor.

00:17:33.891 --> 00:17:35.752
He had someone that became
like a second mom to him

00:17:35.752 --> 00:17:37.462
who told him, "Yes, you're ready.

00:17:37.462 --> 00:17:38.458
"Yes, you're ready."

00:17:38.458 --> 00:17:40.152
He went to that event two weeks in.

00:17:40.152 --> 00:17:43.005
He won that, he qualified
for the world championship.

00:17:43.005 --> 00:17:44.354
And then he's like, "I qualified there,

00:17:44.354 --> 00:17:45.860
"but this is the world.

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:47.290
"Everybody from the world is coming in.

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:49.012
"I can't do this, I'm too young."

00:17:49.012 --> 00:17:51.141
He started going through
all these excuses.

00:17:51.141 --> 00:17:52.768
And then, like all entrepreneurs do,

00:17:52.768 --> 00:17:56.078
so I want you to know, we all
think the same things you do.

00:17:56.078 --> 00:17:58.681
And all the things that are there,

00:17:58.681 --> 00:18:00.254
are there for everybody.

00:18:00.254 --> 00:18:03.080
But one difference is: overcome your fear

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:05.112
and step it up and jump in the game,

00:18:05.112 --> 00:18:07.798
because, listen, Wayne Gretzky said,

00:18:07.798 --> 00:18:09.862
"You miss 100% of the
shots you don't take."

00:18:09.862 --> 00:18:11.936
He wanted to wait a whole nother year.

00:18:11.936 --> 00:18:14.026
When he went into the competition,

00:18:14.026 --> 00:18:16.313
they had him ranked that he would finish

00:18:16.313 --> 00:18:17.543
fifth through seventh.

00:18:17.543 --> 00:18:18.828
And he jumped in.

00:18:18.828 --> 00:18:20.231
He did the performances of his life.

00:18:20.231 --> 00:18:22.052
And he won the world championship.

00:18:22.052 --> 00:18:24.323
Feeling he wasn't ready.

00:18:24.323 --> 00:18:25.648
Completely didn't want to do it.

00:18:25.648 --> 00:18:29.342
Think about how his life
probably changed forever,

00:18:29.342 --> 00:18:33.391
forever and ever, because he
actually overcame that fear,

00:18:33.391 --> 00:18:35.968
didn't listen to that
demon, those voices inside,

00:18:35.968 --> 00:18:37.156
telling him he wasn't ready.

00:18:37.156 --> 00:18:39.228
And he got in the game.

00:18:39.228 --> 00:18:42.767
And I want you to think about
future-proofing your life.

00:18:42.767 --> 00:18:44.461
What does that mean?

00:18:44.461 --> 00:18:47.203
You know, technology is
moving so fast right now.

00:18:47.203 --> 00:18:49.510
I was just at an event last
week with Peter Diamandis,

00:18:49.510 --> 00:18:51.418
the author of Abundance.

00:18:51.418 --> 00:18:53.176
He's the creator of the X Prize.

00:18:53.176 --> 00:18:56.450
He was the one that put up
the money for the first ship

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:58.976
that went into orbit
that wasn't part of NASA

00:18:58.976 --> 00:19:00.503
or part of a government.

00:19:00.503 --> 00:19:01.826
The guy is just unbelievable.

00:19:01.826 --> 00:19:03.078
He's such a visionary

00:19:03.078 --> 00:19:04.282
and showed where we're going.

00:19:04.282 --> 00:19:06.808
Right now there's 100 cars in Pittsburgh,

00:19:06.808 --> 00:19:08.092
Ubers that are driving themselves.

00:19:08.092 --> 00:19:09.629
They're driverless cars.

00:19:09.629 --> 00:19:11.461
Ford is making driverless cars.

00:19:11.461 --> 00:19:14.603
They're thinking that Uber
alone, in six or seven years,

00:19:14.603 --> 00:19:16.148
will be 100% driverless.

00:19:16.148 --> 00:19:18.217
There's a million Uber drivers.

00:19:18.217 --> 00:19:19.416
Technology, right now,

00:19:19.416 --> 00:19:21.046
robots are going to be cleaning our house,

00:19:21.046 --> 00:19:22.471
not in 100 years, like in 10.

00:19:22.471 --> 00:19:24.690
Robots are taking over factories.

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:27.970
So what that means is a lot
of jobs are going to be lost.

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:29.346
A lot of scarcity.

00:19:29.346 --> 00:19:30.706
A lot of people getting scared.

00:19:30.706 --> 00:19:31.799
Uncertain times.

00:19:31.799 --> 00:19:35.642
But really, the foundation of all success

00:19:35.642 --> 00:19:37.815
isn't the magic widget,

00:19:37.815 --> 00:19:39.738
the magic pill that gets you rich,

00:19:39.738 --> 00:19:41.226
the lucky invention.

00:19:41.226 --> 00:19:43.936
All success starts with our habits.

00:19:43.936 --> 00:19:48.449
All successful people don't
worry about the change,

00:19:48.449 --> 00:19:49.547
they embrace it.

00:19:49.547 --> 00:19:50.443
They want it.

00:19:50.443 --> 00:19:52.243
Peter Diamandis is onstage and saying,

00:19:52.243 --> 00:19:53.868
"Do you see how amazing this is?"

00:19:53.868 --> 00:19:55.251
But what you have to think about is

00:19:55.251 --> 00:19:57.004
how do you future-proof your life?

00:19:57.004 --> 00:19:58.780
How do you future-proof your income?

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:00.963
What are some of the
things that you can do

00:20:00.963 --> 00:20:04.252
to make sure you're in a
job that's sustainable?

00:20:04.252 --> 00:20:06.197
You create a business that's sustainable.

00:20:06.197 --> 00:20:10.519
All of those are kind of, to me, abundant.

00:20:10.519 --> 00:20:11.619
They're everywhere,

00:20:11.619 --> 00:20:12.624
but what happens is,

00:20:12.624 --> 00:20:14.528
when you back up five or six steps,

00:20:14.528 --> 00:20:16.057
that's where it all starts.

00:20:16.057 --> 00:20:18.264
It all starts with an abundant mindset.

00:20:18.264 --> 00:20:20.540
It all starts with having
a vision and clarity

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:22.462
in what you really want out of your life.

00:20:22.462 --> 00:20:24.658
It all starts with not
working on your weaknesses

00:20:24.658 --> 00:20:26.043
and gaining your confidence.

00:20:26.043 --> 00:20:29.431
It all starts with
knowing why you want more.

00:20:29.431 --> 00:20:34.060
And it starts with having
the habits that make you,

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:37.902
not overcome, but thrive
during these uncertain times.

00:20:37.902 --> 00:20:40.440
Stop worrying about technology.

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:44.589
Stop worrying about the crazy
politicians in today's world.

00:20:44.589 --> 00:20:46.926
Stop letting the news affect you.

00:20:46.926 --> 00:20:49.896
Stop letting the outside
world control your knobs,

00:20:49.896 --> 00:20:51.272
turn you up, turn you down.

00:20:51.272 --> 00:20:53.066
You can future-proof
your life by not letting

00:20:53.066 --> 00:20:56.102
those thoughts that the future is bad

00:20:56.102 --> 00:20:57.929
live inside your head.

00:20:57.929 --> 00:20:59.948
If we focus on what could go wrong,

00:20:59.948 --> 00:21:03.734
if we focus on robots and
technology taking our job,

00:21:03.734 --> 00:21:05.390
we get small.

00:21:05.390 --> 00:21:08.187
What I want you to start doing
is think how you can go big,

00:21:08.187 --> 00:21:09.879
how you can open up and say,

00:21:09.879 --> 00:21:12.235
"What is this amazing technology?"

00:21:12.235 --> 00:21:14.229
A billion people are
going to be coming online

00:21:14.229 --> 00:21:15.346
over the next 10 years.

00:21:15.346 --> 00:21:16.436
All these changes.

00:21:16.436 --> 00:21:17.691
This amazing technology,

00:21:17.691 --> 00:21:19.558
how can you step out in front of it?

00:21:19.558 --> 00:21:23.364
How can you be a part of
something people always need?

00:21:23.364 --> 00:21:27.682
How can you look at it through
glasses where it's half-full?

00:21:27.682 --> 00:21:31.561
Where you can look at it
through an abundance state,

00:21:31.561 --> 00:21:33.210
rather than a scarcity state.

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:34.861
Life is going to happen anyway.

00:21:34.861 --> 00:21:36.957
Technology is going to happen anyway.

00:21:36.957 --> 00:21:38.859
We can focus on what's wrong with it,

00:21:38.859 --> 00:21:39.781
or how can it hurt us.

00:21:39.781 --> 00:21:41.105
And that's how we feel.

00:21:41.105 --> 00:21:42.000
That's how we act,

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:43.430
and that's what we get.

00:21:43.430 --> 00:21:45.585
Or we can find a way to
find abundance out of it.

00:21:45.585 --> 00:21:46.830
Find joy out of it.

00:21:46.830 --> 00:21:48.480
Find excitement about the future.

00:21:48.480 --> 00:21:51.319
And with that, you will find the path

00:21:51.319 --> 00:21:52.567
that will create wealth,

00:21:52.567 --> 00:21:53.415
will create joy.

00:21:53.415 --> 00:21:54.793
If you're one of my real estate students,

00:21:54.793 --> 00:21:56.709
everybody will always need real estate.

00:21:56.709 --> 00:21:57.822
If you're not in real estate,

00:21:57.822 --> 00:21:59.079
whatever it is you do,

00:21:59.079 --> 00:22:00.080
find the angle.

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:01.161
If you're in the life coaching business,

00:22:01.161 --> 00:22:03.135
everybody will always need life coaching.

00:22:03.135 --> 00:22:04.325
High performance coaching.

00:22:04.325 --> 00:22:07.625
That's two of a million
things you could be doing

00:22:07.625 --> 00:22:09.005
that are future-proof.

00:22:09.005 --> 00:22:11.109
But the biggest thing I
wanted to share today,

00:22:11.109 --> 00:22:14.229
what really future-proofing
your life means,

00:22:14.229 --> 00:22:16.060
is having the right state of mind.

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:17.863
Being the observer of your thoughts,

00:22:17.863 --> 00:22:20.013
and find a way to focus on the future,

00:22:20.013 --> 00:22:24.096
not dragging that anchor
of your past behind you.

