00:23:05.174 --> 00:23:08.094
- Is there a formula to the
most successful infomercial,

00:23:08.094 --> 00:23:10.842
like five or six things
that you must have?

00:23:10.842 --> 00:23:12.339
- You know what's so funny when

00:23:12.339 --> 00:23:13.513
I went dead before.

00:23:13.513 --> 00:23:16.464
When there was a thought I
had and that never happens,

00:23:16.464 --> 00:23:17.450
cause I just got off a plane.

00:23:17.450 --> 00:23:18.790
It might be the Dramamine.

00:23:18.790 --> 00:23:20.730
But I went flat for a second

00:23:20.730 --> 00:23:22.047
cause what I was thinking,

00:23:22.047 --> 00:23:22.880
what I was going to tell you is

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:24.804
you said, "How did you
know it was going to work?"

00:23:24.804 --> 00:23:26.246
And, what I'd share with anybody watching,

00:23:26.246 --> 00:23:27.523
in any kind of marketing,

00:23:27.523 --> 00:23:28.636
or any kind of persuasion,

00:23:28.636 --> 00:23:31.761
or attracting somebody,
persuading somebody,

00:23:31.761 --> 00:23:33.139
get them to take action,

00:23:33.139 --> 00:23:35.451
when I look back at those
original infomercials,

00:23:35.451 --> 00:23:36.921
I had two things going for me.

00:23:36.921 --> 00:23:38.838
I wasn't the smartest guy in the world,

00:23:38.838 --> 00:23:42.751
struggled reading, insecure about that.

00:23:42.751 --> 00:23:43.890
Wasn't college-educated.

00:23:43.890 --> 00:23:46.607
I don't have a really
incredible vocabulary.

00:23:46.607 --> 00:23:48.557
It's hard for me to
articulate certain words

00:23:48.557 --> 00:23:51.237
cause they're just not in there, right?

00:23:51.237 --> 00:23:54.741
But what I had was
enthusiasm and authenticity.

00:23:54.741 --> 00:23:56.538
When I look back at those infomercials,

00:23:56.538 --> 00:23:58.377
and they hit like monsters.

00:23:58.377 --> 00:24:02.294
One infomercial I did
did 150 million in sales.

00:24:04.532 --> 00:24:05.499
- Wow.

00:24:05.499 --> 00:24:06.812
- Just one infomercial.

00:24:06.812 --> 00:24:09.279
- How long of a period was that over?

00:24:09.279 --> 00:24:10.341
- About 18 months.

00:24:10.341 --> 00:24:11.883
- Wow, that's amazing.

00:24:11.883 --> 00:24:13.445
- And I look back at that,

00:24:13.445 --> 00:24:14.577
and I don't say that to brag,

00:24:14.577 --> 00:24:15.758
all that's not profit.

00:24:15.758 --> 00:24:17.007
- Of course.

00:24:17.007 --> 00:24:19.817
You spend a lot on media, of course.

00:24:19.817 --> 00:24:21.583
- I barely say anything about money.

00:24:21.583 --> 00:24:23.416
I'm saying it to make an impact.

00:24:23.416 --> 00:24:24.968
Because I wasn't the smartest guy.

00:24:24.968 --> 00:24:25.883
I didn't go to college.

00:24:25.883 --> 00:24:27.031
I didn't come from anything.

00:24:27.031 --> 00:24:28.994
Most people watching are way further ahead

00:24:28.994 --> 00:24:30.087
than I was when I started.

00:24:30.087 --> 00:24:31.319
- You weren't trained on the camera.

00:24:31.319 --> 00:24:32.152
You weren't--

00:24:32.152 --> 00:24:33.116
- But what I did have,

00:24:33.116 --> 00:24:35.020
as I look back even at those old shows,

00:24:35.020 --> 00:24:36.514
where I'm embarrassed to see myself

00:24:36.514 --> 00:24:38.194
and my New York accent was super-heavy,

00:24:38.194 --> 00:24:39.266
that's where I grew up,

00:24:39.266 --> 00:24:42.805
is I had authenticity and enthusiasm.

00:24:42.805 --> 00:24:45.894
And I think people could see
this guy really wants to help.

00:24:45.894 --> 00:24:46.857
It wasn't scripted.

00:24:46.857 --> 00:24:47.797
It wasn't perfect.

00:24:47.797 --> 00:24:48.758
I stuttered.

00:24:48.758 --> 00:24:50.537
I said words wrong.

00:24:50.537 --> 00:24:51.659
I look at some of those,

00:24:51.659 --> 00:24:53.273
I used the wrong words
in the wrong context.

00:24:53.273 --> 00:24:55.011
But it still converted.

00:24:55.011 --> 00:24:59.178
And as I evolved and the
first time I did a sit-down

00:25:00.376 --> 00:25:01.930
Larry King-style infomercial,

00:25:01.930 --> 00:25:03.537
he's the one that gave
me the idea for that.

00:25:03.537 --> 00:25:05.145
Then I did the one where
I was driving in my car.

00:25:05.145 --> 00:25:07.271
The reason I did that
driving in my car was

00:25:07.271 --> 00:25:10.638
I wanted people to know that
I wasn't using a teleprompter,

00:25:10.638 --> 00:25:11.911
there wasn't somebody scripting me,

00:25:11.911 --> 00:25:12.926
there wasn't a million cuts,

00:25:12.926 --> 00:25:13.759
it was just me just driving.

00:25:13.759 --> 00:25:14.737
- Wasn't produced, yeah.

00:25:14.737 --> 00:25:15.570
- Wasn't produced.

00:25:15.570 --> 00:25:17.428
It was me driving from my office,

00:25:17.428 --> 00:25:18.708
I started it with a backpack.

00:25:18.708 --> 00:25:19.541
I said, "I'm going home.

00:25:19.541 --> 00:25:20.374
"You want to take a ride with me?"

00:25:20.374 --> 00:25:21.693
And I talked until I got home.

00:25:21.693 --> 00:25:25.696
Briana and my son were
probably three and one.

00:25:25.696 --> 00:25:26.655
When I got to the door,

00:25:26.655 --> 00:25:27.488
they came running out.

00:25:27.488 --> 00:25:28.768
That was the end of the infomercial.

00:25:28.768 --> 00:25:29.727
- That's cool.

00:25:29.727 --> 00:25:30.776
- And that wasn't even planned.

00:25:30.776 --> 00:25:32.098
They just ran out cause
Dad was home, right?

00:25:32.098 --> 00:25:32.931
- Wow.

00:25:33.829 --> 00:25:35.544
- But I did that because I could tell

00:25:35.544 --> 00:25:37.845
the authenticity and the enthusiasm I had

00:25:37.845 --> 00:25:39.717
to change people's lives was there.

00:25:39.717 --> 00:25:41.849
I want other people in
my field to step it up

00:25:41.849 --> 00:25:44.979
and do better cause it'll
always keep me on my toes.

00:25:44.979 --> 00:25:46.579
I want my competitors
to step up their game.

00:25:46.579 --> 00:25:48.487
When I get frustrated with my competitors,

00:25:48.487 --> 00:25:49.785
it's because they're slacking.

00:25:49.785 --> 00:25:51.827
They're teaching five year old strategies.

00:25:51.827 --> 00:25:53.198
They're hands-off.

00:25:53.198 --> 00:25:54.350
They do an infomercial

00:25:54.350 --> 00:25:55.534
and let someone else run the education.

00:25:55.534 --> 00:25:56.675
I hate all that crap.

00:25:56.675 --> 00:25:58.644
I would love for them to be as good as us.

00:25:58.644 --> 00:26:00.615
I would love for somebody
to get close to me

00:26:00.615 --> 00:26:02.354
because all I do is get more competitive

00:26:02.354 --> 00:26:03.499
and get better and better.

00:26:03.499 --> 00:26:05.303
Competition is great.

00:26:05.303 --> 00:26:07.275
I can remember thinking,

00:26:07.275 --> 00:26:09.978
throughout high school
and even in my early 20s,

00:26:09.978 --> 00:26:11.334
maybe not my early 20s,

00:26:11.334 --> 00:26:13.207
I flipped pretty quick.

00:26:13.207 --> 00:26:14.363
But right around 20 years old--

00:26:14.363 --> 00:26:15.661
- You didn't go to college, right?

00:26:15.661 --> 00:26:16.500
- No, I didn't go to college.

00:26:16.500 --> 00:26:17.562
I barely got out of high school.

00:26:17.562 --> 00:26:18.564
- Right.

00:26:18.564 --> 00:26:20.471
- But I can remember
thinking in high school,

00:26:20.471 --> 00:26:22.783
whatever years that was,

00:26:22.783 --> 00:26:25.561
I hope someday I can get a job

00:26:25.561 --> 00:26:27.102
and make a thousand bucks a week

00:26:27.102 --> 00:26:28.197
and just get by.

00:26:28.197 --> 00:26:29.136
I'm not that smart

00:26:29.136 --> 00:26:29.969
cause I had trouble reading

00:26:29.969 --> 00:26:30.922
I still can't read great.

00:26:30.922 --> 00:26:32.310
I had dyslexia,

00:26:32.310 --> 00:26:34.113
is what I think it's been diagnosed now.

00:26:34.113 --> 00:26:36.662
But I still can't
comprehend good when I read,

00:26:36.662 --> 00:26:39.526
but I didn't realize I was an
audible and visual learner.

00:26:39.526 --> 00:26:40.466
I can listen to a book,

00:26:40.466 --> 00:26:41.299
and I'll memorize the whole book.

00:26:41.299 --> 00:26:42.132
- Wow.

00:26:42.132 --> 00:26:42.965
- I could watch somebody onstage

00:26:42.965 --> 00:26:44.880
and emulate that if it fits my life,

00:26:44.880 --> 00:26:47.501
but sometimes we're judged by a scorecard

00:26:47.501 --> 00:26:49.167
that's an outdated scorecard, right?

00:26:49.167 --> 00:26:51.426
So not only did we not have money,

00:26:51.426 --> 00:26:54.212
I also felt, well I'm not
smart enough to go to school.

00:26:54.212 --> 00:26:57.791
And something changed
around 17, 18 years old.

00:26:57.791 --> 00:27:00.672
Something flipped and I noticed,

00:27:00.672 --> 00:27:02.529
and this is going to sound
like it's a pitch for the book,

00:27:02.529 --> 00:27:03.362
and it's not.

00:27:03.362 --> 00:27:04.986
But I noticed people in my town,

00:27:04.986 --> 00:27:06.504
this little tiny town I
grew up in upstate New York,

00:27:06.504 --> 00:27:08.169
the people that had money,

00:27:08.169 --> 00:27:10.070
the people that seemed happier,

00:27:10.070 --> 00:27:11.346
I don't know behind the scenes,

00:27:11.346 --> 00:27:13.408
but they seemed happier, more fulfilled,

00:27:13.408 --> 00:27:14.826
they were more relaxed,

00:27:14.826 --> 00:27:18.166
like they were walking
up a ladder instead of

00:27:18.166 --> 00:27:20.219
my family seemed like they
were running on a treadmill.

00:27:20.219 --> 00:27:22.147
It's like we're going fast,

00:27:22.147 --> 00:27:23.167
but we're not going anywhere.

00:27:23.167 --> 00:27:26.000
So why is this guy or this woman
in this town doing so well?

00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:28.085
And I remember just obsessing on it.

00:27:28.085 --> 00:27:30.708
And what I noticed was,

00:27:30.708 --> 00:27:32.420
I didn't call it habits,

00:27:32.420 --> 00:27:33.686
I'd love to say I figured this out

00:27:33.686 --> 00:27:34.519
when I was in my 20s,

00:27:34.519 --> 00:27:36.071
but what I realized is they
just did different things

00:27:36.071 --> 00:27:37.940
than my family and my friends were doing.

00:27:37.940 --> 00:27:40.120
And I just started obsessing on that.

00:27:40.120 --> 00:27:41.649
And I was young enough and naive enough

00:27:41.649 --> 00:27:43.719
to just think I could do it.

00:27:43.719 --> 00:27:46.059
I mean, sometimes you wish
you could give that gift

00:27:46.059 --> 00:27:48.741
to somebody in their 20s,
30s, 50s, 70s, right?

00:27:48.741 --> 00:27:51.704
I had the gift of being
naive and a little dumb

00:27:51.704 --> 00:27:53.385
and not listening to anybody.

00:27:53.385 --> 00:27:56.400
In 1998, I did my first infomercial.

00:27:56.400 --> 00:27:57.620
- Wow.

00:27:57.620 --> 00:27:59.179
Almost 20 years ago.

00:27:59.179 --> 00:28:02.345
- Yeah, 1998, I filmed my first one.

00:28:02.345 --> 00:28:04.271
And my sister, my daughter's aunt,

00:28:04.271 --> 00:28:05.434
my daughter's sitting here with us,

00:28:05.434 --> 00:28:07.663
my sister drove from Virginia,

00:28:07.663 --> 00:28:08.671
because by then,

00:28:08.671 --> 00:28:10.754
in 1998 I had apartments,

00:28:12.099 --> 00:28:13.679
I had a collision shop,

00:28:13.679 --> 00:28:14.826
I had an auto sales,

00:28:14.826 --> 00:28:16.762
and I was building houses

00:28:16.762 --> 00:28:18.331
From that broke kid,

00:28:18.331 --> 00:28:19.644
I was doing well.

00:28:19.644 --> 00:28:20.517
- How old when you started that?

00:28:20.517 --> 00:28:22.517
- 1998 was 20 years ago.

00:28:23.652 --> 00:28:25.891
I was 28, 29 years old.

00:28:25.891 --> 00:28:26.724
- Wow.

